From: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mt_wifi_osal: Handle void init_dummy_netdev()

init_dummy_netdev() returns void in newer kernels. Call it and return
zero from the OSAL wrapper, retaining the old return path for older
kernels.

Signed-off-by: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
--- a/mt_osal_net.c
+++ b/mt_osal_net.c
@@ -669,7 +669,12 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL(mt_os_net_dev_get_iw_stats
 
 int mt_init_dummy_netdev(struct net_device *dev)
 {
+#if KERNEL_VERSION(6, 9, 0) <= LINUX_VERSION_CODE
+	init_dummy_netdev(dev);
+	return 0;
+#else
 	return init_dummy_netdev(dev);
+#endif
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(mt_init_dummy_netdev);
 
